  message: "D-enum + scala-enum owner emission LANDED (PR #48, dev f4fecdb613): d_lang.py _process_enum_declaration + enum_declaration dispatch; scala.py enum_definition case -> both emit kind='enum' owners so the containment linker (enum in CONTAINER_KINDS) roots the enum members/body-fields (Color.red, Color.rgb) instead of orphaning them. Evidence: test_enum_members_emitted_as_fields (D) + test_enum_body_val_emits_field (scala) assert the 'Color' kind='enum' owner is emitted; rooting follows from the established enum-container behavior (WI-sakug). RESIDUAL NEEDS OWNER DECISION: the Scala 3 'given' owner. 'given' has no registered symbol kind, so rooting its body fields (intOrd.cached) requires EITHER registering a 'given' symbol kind (ADR-0027 axis addition) OR an explicit ruling to emit it as kind='object' (conflates two constructs, deliberately avoided per one-construct-per-kind). Enum CASES also out of scope. Set needs_human_review pending that ruling."  # 0891
